# ThreadSanitizer suppressions (TSAN_OPTIONS=suppressions=scripts/tsan.supp).
#
# Lock-order inversions inside third-party C libraries, between their own locks, all taken on
# PatchBox's main thread (nothing else in the process calls them), so they can't deadlock here:
# - Berkeley DB, which libjack's metadata uses: one order reading a property, another closing
#   the client;
# - libdbus, which SDL loads: its init and its shutdown.
deadlock:libdb-5.3.so
deadlock:libdbus-1.so
